course: dictionary
lesson: 3332
title: Everyday or every day?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Everyday is one word, and it is an adjective. It describes things that are usual or ordinary, the kind you use or do all the time, like everyday clothes. «Many everyday English words were born in these old stories: panic, odyssey, mentor, echo, cereal and even the month of January.» Here everyday means ordinary words that people use all the time, not rare or special ones.
explain: Two words, every day, mean something different. They mean each day, and they tell you how often something happens. «I practise my spellings every day» tells you the practice happens each day. One word describes a thing; two words tell you when or how often.
explain: Context helps you choose. «The everyday picture and the science picture can both be true.» Everyday here means the ordinary way we see things, and science is a different way of looking. Try swapping in «usual» or «ordinary». If it still makes sense, everyday is the one-word adjective.
fact: Everyday means usual or ordinary, used or done all the time.
fact: «Every day» (two words) means each day.
fact: The cost of living is how much money you need for food, heating, rent and other everyday things.
fact: A parable is a short story Jesus told about everyday life, with a deeper meaning about God and how to live.
fact: Maths tip: total = daily amount × days. Saving 2 pounds every day for 5 days makes 10 pounds.
exercise: «She wears her everyday clothes to school, not her party dress.» What does everyday mean here? | Fancy, only for special days | Brand new and never worn | *Usual or ordinary, worn all the time | Wet and muddy from playing
exercise: Ella writes, «I practise my spellings every day.» What do the two words every day tell us? | *Each day, how often | Only on special days | Something that is wet | Something very old
exercise: Sam saves 2 pounds every day for 5 days. How much does Sam save in total? | 2 pounds | *10 pounds | 7 pounds | 25 pounds
test: Find the word in «The everyday picture and the science picture can both be true.» that means ordinary. | science | both | *everyday | picture
test: Riya washes her hands every day after lunch. What does every day mean? | Only once | *Each day | Ordinary and usual | Very clean
exam: In «A parable is a short story Jesus told about everyday life», what does everyday mean? | *Usual, ordinary life | Very long and difficult | Each day, how often | A special holiday
